  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when your brand-new basement tile starts cracking, right? It's a common issue, and usually, it boils down to a few preventable mistakes during installation. One of the biggest culprits is skipping those crucial moisture checks before installation. Basements can have a lot of moisture, and if it's not managed properly with the right adhesive and underlayment, tiles can fail. Another huge factor is poor surface preparation. If the concrete slab isn't properly cleaned or if cracks aren't repaired, you're building on a weak foundation. Similarly, inadequate adhesive coverage is a big no-no; the tile won't bond properly. Finally, installing on an out-of-flat floor is a recipe for disaster. If your floor has more than a quarter-inch variation over 10 feet, those tiles are going to be under stress and eventually crack. When you're hiring someone, always ask how they handle moisture and what their process is for preparing the subfloor. A good installer will account for these things. If your basement has significant issues like unevenness or high moisture, getting a qualified professional involved upfront can prevent these headaches and save you money in the long run. HH Remodeling LLC is experienced in addressing these challenges in Denver and the surrounding areas.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
